# 詞: 銀包

1. 我今日出門忘記咗帶銀包，搞到連杯咖啡都買唔到。 (I forgot to bring my wallet when I went out today, so I couldn't even buy a cup of coffee.)
2. 你睇下我新買嘅銀包靚唔靚？係皮革製㗎。 (Take a look at my new wallet, isn't it nice? It's made of leather.)
3. 佢成日話自己冇錢，但係我見佢銀包厚過磚頭咁。 (He always says he has no money, but I see his wallet is as thick as a brick.)
4. 小心啲啦，地鐵站人多，容易俾人偷銀包。 (Be careful, there are many people at the MTR station, and it's easy to get your wallet stolen.)
5. 我銀包入面淨係剩低幾蚊零錢，真係窮到喊。 (There are only a few coins left in my wallet; I'm really broke.)
6. 你唔好將銀包放喺後袋，好易跌出嚟㗎。 (Don't put your wallet in your back pocket; it falls out very easily.)
7. 佢揾到一個銀包，即刻交畀警察，真係好人嚟㗎。 (He found a wallet and immediately handed it to the police; he's a really good person.)
8. 我個銀包用咗好多年，皮都甩晒，想換過個新嘅。 (I've used my wallet for many years, and the leather is peeling off, so I want to get a new one.)
9. 你銀包入面有冇身份證？如果唔見咗就麻煩喇。 (Do you have your ID card in your wallet? If you lose it, it'll be troublesome.)
10. 佢話要請食飯，但係掏銀包嗰陣先發現冇帶錢，好尷尬。 (He said he would treat us to a meal, but when he reached for his wallet, he realized he didn't bring any money; it was very awkward.)

完成10句例句 [end of text]


